{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "satisfaction_themes",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly operationalizes the 'satisfaction themes' half of the query, giving a clean multi-label axis to group/aggregate on. Grounding is mostly sound: YLP-0001 praises friendly employees (service_quality) and food, though it flags only service while food is arguably present; YLP-0004 service_quality is well warranted. Values are reasonable readings, with NULL correctly used for silent/negative rows."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_themes",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly addresses the 'complaint themes' half of the query and provides a strong categorical axis. YLP-0002 poor_service is well grounded. Weakness: YLP-0005 (gave away cabana, refused entry, bad drinks, discriminatory) is marked 'none' despite clear complaints, and YLP-0003's price/portion gripe is missed — these are under-extractions rather than invented facts, so groundedness stays fairly high."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment_intensity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A graded sentiment scale is somewhat richer than the existing binary label_pos, offering a finer axis, but it substantially overlaps with label_pos and is only tangential to identifying specific satisfaction/complaint THEMES. Values align well with source tone (very_negative for YLP-0005, positive for YLP-0001)."
    },
    {
      "name": "theme_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.4,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Largely a mechanical roll-up of the two theme columns, adding limited independent analytical leverage for the thematic query. Values are internally consistent with the produced theme columns (e.g., single-theme rows = 1, empty = 0), so groundedness is high even where the underlying theme extraction is debatable."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
  "source_groundedness": 0.84,
  "rationale": "The two theme columns squarely serve the query, providing genuine categorical axes for grouping satisfaction and complaint patterns, and are the analytical core. Sentiment_intensity is a useful but partly redundant refinement of the existing binary label, and theme_count is a derived roll-up with modest added value. Grounding is generally sound extraction/categorisation with appropriate NULLs; no invented facts observed, though there are some under-extractions (e.g., YLP-0005 complaints marked none), which slightly lowers groundedness without constituting hallucination."
}

